WEBVTT

00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:08.190
Attention, all units.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.300
The squadron will now begin laserjagd training.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:15.200
The forwards will be 
Lieutenant Kruger and myself,

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.700
as well as Second Lieutenants 
Krzasińska and Hosenfeld.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.460
The rear will be comprised of 
Lieutenants Pham and Jeckeln,

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.960
as well as Second Lieutenants 
Eberbach and Waldheim.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.590
Second Lieutenant Hosenfeld, 
are you up for this?

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:32.050
There's a less experienced
girl than me trying to fight.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.470
I can't just sit around.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.690
I won't let what happened to Second 
Lieutenant Inghild happen again.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.630
Now, Second Lieutenant Waldheim,

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:43.730
as of today you've been assigned to replenish 
the ranks of the 666th Squadron.

00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:44.620
Right!

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:48.630
I heard you peed your pants during 
your first fight in the West.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.850
H-How did you know that?

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.600
Our squadron's missions are extremely brutal.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.930
Don't make a mess.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:00.270
Second Lieutenant Eberbach,

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:03.610
you will continue to support 
Second Lieutenant Waldheim.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:04.210
Yes.

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:07.250
Th-Thank you, Eberbach!

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:09.170
Wh-Why me?

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:13.670
You will protect Second Lieutenant 
Waldheim. Understood?

00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:17.410
Roger.

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:22.210
All units, move to NOE flight.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:23.790
Roger!

00:02:57.130 --> 00:03:01.860
German Democratic Republic 
Bebersee Base

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:06.920
Good work.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.330
I can't even stand...

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:17.130
<i>Her first time in a Balalaika, 
and she was able to fly that low?</i>

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:20.810
Good work, you two.

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:25.220
You got into another brawl...

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:29.900
I know you think you're good with a knife, 
but that's a bad habit, Theodor.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:32.650
Stop calling me by my first name.

00:03:32.650 --> 00:03:35.900
Aww, now, that just makes me sad.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:38.560
So can I call you "Katia"?

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:40.920
Y-Yes, Lieutenant Pham!

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:42.750
Just call me "Sis."

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:45.250
Well, how did you like the Balalaika?

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:47.590
I was surprised.

00:03:47.590 --> 00:03:49.790
It's not at all like a Phantom.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:54.490
It's more mobile, but as 
a result, less well-armored.

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:56.790
It has flaws all its own.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:01.970
You have talent if you can figure 
that out on your first run.

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:05.620
I'm expecting a lot of you, Katia.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:07.710
Also, be sure to stop peeing your pants, okay?

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:09.810
Not you, too!

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:15.970
Huh? Which unit is that?

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:18.320
No, this sound...

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:23.320
That's a MiG-23 Cheburashka.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:32.080
That coloring... It's the Stasi!

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.340
What are the Stasi doing here?

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.800
How would I know?

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:46.560
<i>Could it be...</i>

00:04:49.130 --> 00:04:51.310
It's been a long time, Iris.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:58.020
What brings Stasi MPs all the way out here, 
Lieutenant Colonel Heinze Axmann?

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:04.900
And Major Beatrix Brehme, 
Commander of the Werewolf Battalion.

00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:08.820
It's been so long since we've seen each 
other, and you're still so cold.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:10.860
You know why we're here.

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:14.080
To have Second Lieutenant Katia Waldheim 
come with us and clarify some things.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:19.610
The second lieutenant followed proper 
procedures for joining our squadron.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:21.500
There's no need to question her.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:23.210
Oh, you don't think so?

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:27.670
Her request for asylum came out of nowhere.

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:31.730
Yet she was approved and taken into 
your squadron with extreme haste.

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:36.770
And the pilot who brought her in is someone 
with whom we have spent time before.

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:39.920
That doesn't seem suspicious to you?

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:45.240
Have you forgotten my face, Theodor Eberbach?

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:54.700
I can't let you question one of my troops 
when they've done nothing wrong.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.060
Isn't that correct, Comrade Lieutenant?

00:05:57.690 --> 00:06:00.010
For the Stasi to act,

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:03.540
their target must be an enemy of 
the state who's broken the law.

00:06:03.540 --> 00:06:05.950
Second Lieutenant Waldheim hasn't—

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:08.670
You sound so grown-up now.

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:09.970
I'm proud of you,

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:13.800
Political Commissar Lieutenant Gretel Jeckeln.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:15.860
I understand why you suspect me,

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:17.850
but this doesn't make sense!

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:20.320
We're supposed to be fighting the BETA.

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:24.190
We can't beat the BETA unless all of humanity 
trusts each other and works togeth—

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:30.950
The people of the West talk differently, I see.

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:35.110
Trust each other and work together?

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:36.760
Are you serious?

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:40.550
I am! If the two Germanys work 
together, the BETA won't—

00:06:40.550 --> 00:06:43.050
I don't like kids with big mouths.

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:45.840
You're a believer in dangerous ideologies.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.630
Maybe I should kill you here.

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:48.800
Stop it, Sylvia!

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:51.860
I'm not...

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:57.100
I apologize for her rude remark.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:07:00.810
But given the short amount of 
time since her asylum,

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.600
I think it's natural that she'd say that.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:08.550
If you still insist on questioning her, 
despite the fact that you have no basis...

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:13.560
Why are you so bent on protecting her?

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.700
Once someone's suspected of being a spy,

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:19.200
it's faster to shoot them than give 
them political indoctrination.

00:07:19.670 --> 00:07:22.620
The second lieutenant is a 
pilot of the 666th Squadron,

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:24.360
and one of my valued troops.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:29.090
This is a good time to tell you all...

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:35.740
It is an undeniable fact that Captain Irisdina 
Bernhard turned in her own brother.

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:41.480
I am the one who took her testimony, 
and allowed her to survive as a hero.

00:07:43.110 --> 00:07:48.530
She killed her own brother 
to prove her innocence.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:55.020
She's a woman who would kill her own family.

00:07:55.020 --> 00:07:58.540
Someday, she will kill all of you, too.

00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:02.290
We shall see you soon, Katia Waldheim.

00:08:03.170 --> 00:08:04.520
Farewell.

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:10.550
Second Lieutenant Eberbach,

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:15.530
if Katia Waldheim is an enemy of the state, 
you will be convicted along with her.

00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:18.580
There won't be a second time. Be ready.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:31.320
What were they trying to do?

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:39.890
So they've started to take action?

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:42.750
I didn't expect to see her, though.

00:08:42.980 --> 00:08:45.020
You know her?

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:47.710
She and I competed to be valedictorian 
at the Officers Academy.

00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:50.200
She's dangerous.

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:55.380
If we are to stand against the BETA threat,

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:58.740
freedom and equality are 
hindrances to humanity.

00:08:58.740 --> 00:09:02.170
We must unite the people under 
a perfect surveillance state,

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:05.480
and pour all our resources 
toward fighting the BETA!

00:09:05.930 --> 00:09:10.260
Only by coming together as one 
can we defeat the BETA!

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:17.090
That's insane.

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:22.670
Once Second Lieutenant Waldheim wakes up,

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:25.930
give her a little political indoctrination.

00:09:25.930 --> 00:09:26.810
Roger.

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:28.960
Second Lieutenant Eberbach...

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:32.730
Take care of her.

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:46.020
Brother!

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:50.190
Brother!

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:05.200
German Democratic Republic 
Zehdenick

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:05.200
The BETA are going to attack again?

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:10.210
The UN and Soviet High Command have sent 
satellite footage, along with a warning.

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:13.380
The BETA have formed an echelon 
within Polish territory.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:16.590
They'll arrive at our absolute defense
line the day after tomorrow.

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:19.020
But after yesterday's attack,

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:22.720
the fortress garrisons are 
at less than 40% strength.

00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:28.230
Without reinforcements, it's possible 
they'll break through the line, and then...

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.360
The cities will become battlegrounds?

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:32.860
And the capital, Berlin, 
would also be endangered?

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:35.490
But there are very few Laser-classes,

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:37.570
and it's possible to wipe 
them out with artillery.

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:41.950
If we can just stall the Grapplers 
and Tanks in the center...

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:43.620
We don't have the manpower.

00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:47.940
Our TSF-readiness level is less than 40%.

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:51.670
And you want us to run into the center 
of a force over thirty thousand strong?

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:53.930
Well...

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:55.630
I will explain.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:11:00.980
Lieutenant Colonel Heinze Axmann, 
Chief of Stasi Operation.

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:05.020
Two TSF battalions from the Stasi will provide

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:09.210
the reinforcements that Major 
Hannibal says are needed.

00:11:09.210 --> 00:11:11.080
There is nothing to worry about.

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:13.970
We want you to fight your hardest.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:19.650
Fight our hardest, huh?

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:23.910
When the Stasi says that, 
it sounds like a bad joke.

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:27.060
But that gives us the manpower we need.

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:29.060
Thank you, Major.

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:34.790
It's our job to enable commanders 
like you to fight your best.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:39.050
But be careful, Captain Bernhard.

00:11:39.620 --> 00:11:40.900
I intend to.

00:11:48.990 --> 00:11:50.610
You look like you have something to say.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:54.450
I can't believe she sold out her family to 
the Stasi, even for the country's sake.

00:11:55.210 --> 00:11:58.940
Why would you trust someone like that?

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:02.200
Do you really think that's true?

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:06.450
If she really did sell out her family,

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:09.240
you'd expect her to do other, 
worse things, as well.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:15.960
But since that day, she's fought proudly 
and nobly on the battlefield.

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:17.990
Major, you can't believe...

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:23.930
Marai, I have a request.

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:27.000
If something happens to me...

00:12:28.550 --> 00:12:30.370
What a pain...

00:12:33.050 --> 00:12:35.030
Lieutenant General Strachwitz?

00:12:36.460 --> 00:12:42.400
I've heard he commanded the 1st Tank Corps 
on the Eastern European Front.

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.480
But nothing more.

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:49.120
I'll look into it for you.

00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:53.620
If you go poking around,
you're just asking to be arrested.

00:12:54.010 --> 00:12:56.800
<i>Why am I doing something so risky?</i>

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:00.710
Is this it?

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:05.270
<i>"February 18, 1976.</i>

00:13:05.270 --> 00:13:09.960
<i>The Warsaw Pact Armies stop the 
BETA advance in the Ukraine.</i>

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:14.350
<i>The key to victory was the commander 
of the East Germany 1st Tank Corps."</i>

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:16.390
<i>What is this?</i>

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:18.900
<i>The name's been blacked out.</i>

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:22.650
<i>Here, too.</i>

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:25.800
<i>This is about Lieutenant 
General Strachwitz, right?</i>

00:13:26.210 --> 00:13:26.970
<i>Why?</i>

00:13:31.400 --> 00:13:32.230
Here it is.

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:36.620
You're in the paper, Dad.

00:13:36.990 --> 00:13:39.040
They're talking about how great you are.

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:42.280
They say it was one of the 
best performances in years,

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:45.550
and the director's talent 
was simply astonishing.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:47.860
That's great, Dad!

00:13:53.150 --> 00:13:54.560
It's the same.

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:58.060
He was erased by the Stasi...

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:06.070
Theodor!

00:14:06.340 --> 00:14:10.070
Sorry for causing you trouble yesterday.

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:17.960
Why are you looking for 
Lieutenant General Strachwitz?

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:19.930
Did you find something?

00:14:20.780 --> 00:14:22.050
There's nothing to find.

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:24.840
All the records have been erased.

00:14:25.620 --> 00:14:27.000
He probably has been, too.

00:14:27.960 --> 00:14:29.620
Don't dig any deeper into this!

00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:31.940
Or the Stasi might get rid of us, as well!

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:34.470
I... I can't do that.

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:35.530
Why?

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:45.330
H-He's my father...

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:50.250
Five years ago,

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:53.870
my father sent me to West Germany.

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:58.800
My father always said that if the 
two Germanys worked together,

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:01.630
we'd never lose to the BETA.

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:04.550
Then the name "Katia Waldheim"...

00:15:05.760 --> 00:15:09.130
If he was erased, that means he 
must have done something!

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:13.160
And now his daughter's looking 
for him, using a fake name.

00:15:13.160 --> 00:15:14.970
What do you think will happen 
if the Stasi find out?

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:16.990
I won't let the Stasi win.

00:15:16.990 --> 00:15:18.730
I want to know the truth!

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:21.860
Stop dreaming.

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:25.440
They'll do anything to erase 
enemies of the state!

00:15:25.810 --> 00:15:27.830
They killed my family.

00:15:27.830 --> 00:15:30.960
If you don't want to die, 
don't waste your time with this.

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:33.080
If you stay in your place, they won't kill you!

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:35.450
That's just running away.

00:15:36.630 --> 00:15:39.650
No matter what you want, 
if you give up, you'll never get it!

00:15:39.650 --> 00:15:41.960
Is that really okay with you, Theodor?

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:46.710
If we spend our whole lives afraid of 
the Stasi, believing in no one,

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:48.660
we'll never beat the BETA!

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:49.970
You...

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:51.960
<i>What's with her?</i>

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:54.040
<i>Is she trying to get reported to the Stasi?</i>

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:58.760
Satellites have spotted a BETA advance.

00:15:58.760 --> 00:16:01.490
TSF squadrons, prepare for immediate launch.

00:16:01.490 --> 00:16:04.980
Repeat, satellites have spotted a BETA advance.

00:16:02.230 --> 00:16:03.690
Damn... Let's go!

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:04.980
R-Right!

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:08.980
All units are filled up!

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:10.940
Fire the engines!

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:14.550
Captain Bernhard has been seated.

00:16:15.050 --> 00:16:16.490
Sealing control unit.

00:16:16.710 --> 00:16:18.740
Initiating seat information transfer.

00:16:19.220 --> 00:16:21.010
Data link on-line.

00:16:21.990 --> 00:16:24.460
Schwarzes-01. Gantry lock deactivated.

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:26.960
All units to weaponry-equip position.

00:16:36.110 --> 00:16:37.920
Weapons received.

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:38.560
Roger.

00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:41.400
All units to catapult position.

00:16:50.500 --> 00:16:53.030
Schwarzes-01. Connected to catapult.

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:55.030
All units are ready to launch.

00:16:57.280 --> 00:17:01.260
We will head for the enemy position, 
along with the Hannibal Battalion.

00:17:01.260 --> 00:17:02.540
We'll strike their center.

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:05.560
This is your first fight, right? 
Don't screw it up.

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:06.790
R-Right!

00:17:07.340 --> 00:17:09.730
<i>I'm staying away from the Stasi.</i>

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:13.180
<i>She's... She's too dangerous.</i>

00:17:14.530 --> 00:17:16.630
<i>Once we're out on the battlefield, 
I should just...</i>

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:30.070
Former Polish People's Republic Territory 
Oder River's Eastern Shore

00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:02.600
Sitrep?

00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:05.350
We lost the data link with 
Thomas Müntzer's battalion!

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:08.700
Major, we're running out of ammo, too!

00:18:09.120 --> 00:18:09.940
Damn it.

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:12.080
Where are our reinforcements?

00:18:12.080 --> 00:18:13.940
Are they just going to let us die?

00:18:24.610 --> 00:18:25.200
Major,

00:18:25.510 --> 00:18:27.210
more enemies from the left flank.

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:27.790
What?

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:30.290
F-Fortress-class!

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:42.180
Idiot! You're too far forward!

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:44.680
Don't be stupid. Just stay put.

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:47.310
We'll be here for a while. Save your energy.

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:48.450
O-Okay!

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:53.170
All right, crush them!

00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:54.450
Attention, all units!

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:56.630
Major?

00:18:56.630 --> 00:18:58.280
A Fortress-class has appeared.

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:02.840
We cannot continue this battle 
without reinforcements.

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:03.780
Reinforcements...

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:07.830
Our unit will now attempt to 
distract the Fortress-class.

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:10.160
Anyone who can still move, retreat at once.

00:19:13.490 --> 00:19:14.430
Major...

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:17.130
Attention, all units.

00:19:17.390 --> 00:19:20.890
We are moving to reinforce 
the Hannibal Battalion.

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:22.300
Roger!

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:25.140
Wait! New orders from HQ.

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:28.890
"Surface forces are withdrawing 
to Fort Neuenhagen.

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:31.060
You are to support them.

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:34.400
This mission will require one pair of TSFs.

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:38.400
You are to send Lieutenant Pham and 
Second Lieutenant Waldheim."

00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:41.500
What? I've never heard of an order like that!

00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:42.910
Shut up, 06.

00:19:44.660 --> 00:19:45.500
I see.

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:48.910
Schwarzes-02 and 07, form up.

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:51.700
Head for Fort Neuenhagen.

00:19:52.110 --> 00:19:52.920
Roger.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:54.690
You sure about this?

00:19:54.690 --> 00:19:56.210
They both might—

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:57.780
Stop it, Anett.

00:19:57.780 --> 00:19:59.940
They'll start to suspect your political loyalties.

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:02.090
You're really okay with this?!

00:20:02.670 --> 00:20:03.930
That's the order.

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:06.310
We will now begin the mission.

00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:07.580
I'm counting on you, Pham.

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:08.530
Roger.

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:11.790
Don't die, Second Lieutenant Katia Waldheim.

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:12.930
I'll do my best.

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:18.070
Theodor...

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:20.000
I'll see you later.

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:35.040
I'm sorry, Marai.

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:39.340
Major!

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:48.640
German Democratic Republic 
Fort Neuenhagen

00:20:52.220 --> 00:20:52.890
Damn it!

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:58.090
We're here to support you.

00:20:58.090 --> 00:20:59.350
Hurry up and go!

00:20:59.350 --> 00:21:00.400
Thanks.

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:05.820
The two of us can't possibly stop them alone.

00:21:05.820 --> 00:21:07.610
Just hit the Grapplers.

00:21:08.070 --> 00:21:09.670
Right, Lieutenant Pham.

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:11.290
"Sis."

00:21:11.670 --> 00:21:15.140
I told you to call me "Sis," Katia.

00:21:15.810 --> 00:21:18.290
R-Right, Sis!

00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:20.790
<i>I won't lose.</i>

00:21:20.790 --> 00:21:22.460
<i>I'll come back alive.</i>

00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:26.010
Behind you, Katia!

00:23:18.770 --> 00:23:20.250
Information has come in.

00:23:20.640 --> 00:23:24.670
Both 02 and 07 had their units badly damaged.

00:23:24.670 --> 00:23:25.500
And those two?

00:23:26.100 --> 00:23:27.130
They're alive.

00:23:27.490 --> 00:23:28.200
But...

00:23:33.440 --> 00:23:34.690
Sis?

00:23:35.450 --> 00:23:36.760
You're awake?

00:23:39.190 --> 00:23:41.270
Um, where are we?

00:23:42.280 --> 00:23:45.020
Fort Neuenhagen...

00:23:45.910 --> 00:23:47.580
The middle of Hell.

00:23:48.050 --> 00:23:54.030
<b>To Be Continued</b>
